                      (        rogue.asm):00001         * Disassembly by L. Curtis Boyle
                      (        rogue.asm):00002         * Edition 1 changes by LCB
                      (        rogue.asm):00003         * 12/18/2017 - changed gfx font mode check to allow gfx font on ANY graphics window
                      (        rogue.asm):00004         *   to         - optimized some code to be smaller/faster.
                      (        rogue.asm):00005         * ??/??/2018   - changed some time delays to use F$Sleep calls (more multi-tasking friendly)
                      (        rogue.asm):00006         * To do:
                      (        rogue.asm):00007         * 1) Fix bug when running on 25 line screens (unecessary scrolling)
                      (        rogue.asm):00008         * 2) Fix 25 line height with smaller width windows (can use extra line for status,etc.)
                      (        rogue.asm):00009         * 3) Add command line option for font # -f=hh
                      (        rogue.asm):00010         * 4) Change hard coded PIA sound to either <CTRL>-<G> or SS.Tone (smaller,
                      (        rogue.asm):00011         *    more multi-tasking friendly
                      (        rogue.asm):00012         * Possible extensions:
                      (        rogue.asm):00013         * 1) Make extended 224 char font so that monsters can be 8x8 graphics
                      (        rogue.asm):00014         * 2) Add option for 106 width (if -f=hh font is 6 bit wide) map
                      (        rogue.asm):00015         * 3) If someone gets creative, add termcap support to run over serial port
                      (        rogue.asm):00016         * 4) Allow it run on VDG screen (32x16 is well within the minimum window size)
                      (        rogue.asm):00017         * Note: Rogue defaults to a 19 byte data aread ($00-$12)
                      (        rogue.asm):00018         * Note 2: It rarely uses DP - should change it, after we see if there is a page that
                      (        rogue.asm):00019         *  is used often.
